@ops = http://localhost:4004/operations

### 1) Should FAIL: ETD before ETA
POST {{ops}}/VesselCalls
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "callNumber": "VC-2026-0101",
  "vessel_ID": "c1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
  "voyageNumber": "MS28",
  "shippingLine_ID": "b1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
  "agent_ID": "b1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
  "eta": "2026-11-20T10:00:00Z",
  "etd": "2026-11-19T10:00:00Z"
}

### 2) Should FAIL with TWO errors at once (req.error collects): bad ETD + bad allocation inside deep insert
POST {{ops}}/VesselCalls
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "callNumber": "VC-2026-0102",
  "vessel_ID": "c1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
  "voyageNumber": "MS29",
  "shippingLine_ID": "b1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001",
  "agent_ID": "b1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003",
  "eta": "2026-11-22T10:00:00Z",
  "etd": "2026-11-21T10:00:00Z",
  "berthAllocations": [
    { "berth_ID": "a1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003", "fromTime": "2026-11-22T12:00:00Z", "toTime": "2026-11-22T08:00:00Z" }
  ]
}

### 3) Should FAIL: PATCH only the ETD to a time before the stored ETA (tests effectiveValues)
PATCH {{ops}}/VesselCalls(d1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002)
Content-Type: application/json

{ "etd": "2026-11-14T00:00:00Z" }

### 4) Should SUCCEED: valid PATCH
PATCH {{ops}}/VesselCalls(d1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002)
Content-Type: application/json

{ "etd": "2026-11-17T06:00:00Z" }

### 5) Read-only master data: should FAIL (405)
DELETE {{ops}}/Vessels(c1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001)